 his ownership KIRO leaves and  goes to his friend katya's house he  explains his ordeal to the guy while  looking up his property papers on the  internet after collecting evidence of  everything he takes it to the National  cooperation the following day just when  he thinks the confusion is about to be  solved he learns that the government  office doesn't have any record of his  name in the office's database kierol  then goes to his office to look for  proof of ownership but no one seems to  recognize him even the people who were  praising him the night before for  creating the game Furious kiril creates  a scene in his office and has to be  kicked out soon he turns to his friend  Katya as he is the only person who still  recognizes him Katya is also confused by  what's happening to KIRO and suggests he  meet his parents to confirm his identity  kiril goes to meet his father but to his  disappointment even he refuses to  recognize him claiming that he doesn't  have any children upset Carol decides to  confront Rina the woman that seemingly  started it all he barges into his former  home and again asks her to leave this  naturally turns into an argument and  kiril threatens her with a knife Rina  remains unfazed as she strangely makes  Carol point the knife to her stomach  Carol thinks she is trying to scare him  but is surprised when she actually stabs  herself in the stomach as Carol tries to  make sense of what just happened Rina  dies soon the police arrive and arrest  kiril on the charge of murdering Rina  the scene finally Cuts back to the  present strangely enough instead of  taking Carol to the police station the  police let him walk away without filing  any charges he then receives a text  message on his phone instructing him to  go to a nearby Lighthouse because he is  stranded in the street at night he  decides to follow the instructions the  lighthouse is in shambles and Carol  spends the night inside of it the  following day when he wakes up he finds  t